                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1462-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="1462-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Sony C800GPAC</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Multi-Pattern Tube Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Sony C800G is a high-end tube vocal microphone. The mic was made popular for pop and R&amp;B production by users like Dr. Dre, Mariah Carey, R. Kelly, Kelly Clarkson and many others.</p><p>Sony&#8217;s C800G capsule is based on the Neumann K67 design. Both are large-diaphragm, dual-diaphragm, center-terminated capsules; the C800G capsule retains the K67&#8217;s characteristic backplate drilling pattern.</p><p>The mic uses a 6AU6 tube in the body, with a large peltier external heatsink to keep the tube at the optimal temperature. Interestingly, the power supply uses an additional two 6AU6 tubes (as rectifiers).</p><p>The mic ships with:</p><ul><li>AC-MC800G (AC Power Supply Unit)</li><li>Wind screen (1)</li><li>Cradle suspension (1)</li><li>Stand screw adator (PF1/2 to NS5/8) (1)</li><li>Stand screw adaptor (PF1/2 to W3/8) (1)</li><li>Mic cable (8m, JIS CNR-01 type, 7-pin) (1)</li><li>Carrying case (1)</li><li>G sticker (1)</li><li>Frequency response chart (2)</li></ul><p><p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Sony/C800G">Sony C800GPAC</a> is also known as: C-800G, C800G.</p>
